    {
      "id": "x0VX7Oyyo0su0LS0GP_-E",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5447.150942234572,
      "y": 317.1659806785119,
      "width": 1004.079345703125,
      "height": 860,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 80,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 333826497,
      "version": 2186,
      "versionNonce": 894773071,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1750486740107,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Concurrency cases and flow\n\n1. user click twice or some how get 2 request \n2. -> idempotency -> sessionId -> \n       same -> reject\n       expire -> reject. \n3.  two user came click on same seat and start booking -> send request to backend\n     -> redirect to payment page with bookingId. -> call third party -> third party -> \n     send us the status via webhook\n\nbooking request , concurrent user: -> add booking entry -> call payment service -> that \n add entry -> return success -> return success with pending status. \n\n\n    -> >1 users trying to book one seat. \n       1. pessimistic ->\n            block on row in database.\n            second person's requiest will either block or timeout or fail. \n         -> flow -> create the booking, mark seat unavailable, -> do in transaction with isolation serialize.\n         -> concurrent user trasaction will block until first on success, and eventually timeout or fail, because seat is unavailable. \n         -> On UI -> perspective -> user will send the book seat request, but either will get timeout or get fail status. \n             \n\n\n          Optimisation: \n            -> block row, but maintain in redis also, mark that seat unavailabe for 1 mins. \n            -> concurrent request will see if that seat is lock or not. if lock rejec.t\n            -> on ui in that period user will see seat unavaiable.  \n       \n\n      2. optimistic:\n           maintain version column in  seat table. \n             -> read -> do transaction for adding , but add check that version sshould be same \n                with initial else fail. \n             -> problematic in case of many users -> they will try to update and fail -> no blocking here. \n\n            -> maintain the version in row\n            -> allow seat booking but fail at time of updation.  \n             \n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Concurrency cases and flow\n\n1. user click twice or some how get 2 request \n2. -> idempotency -> sessionId -> \n       same -> reject\n       expire -> reject. \n3.  two user came click on same seat and start booking -> send request to backend\n     -> redirect to payment page with bookingId. -> call third party -> third party -> \n     send us the status via webhook\n\nbooking request , concurrent user: -> add booking entry -> call payment service -> that \n add entry -> return success -> return success with pending status. \n\n\n    -> >1 users trying to book one seat. \n       1. pessimistic ->\n            block on row in database.\n            second person's requiest will either block or timeout or fail. \n         -> flow -> create the booking, mark seat unavailable, -> do in transaction with isolation serialize.\n         -> concurrent user trasaction will block until first on success, and eventually timeout or fail, because seat is unavailable. \n         -> On UI -> perspective -> user will send the book seat request, but either will get timeout or get fail status. \n             \n\n\n          Optimisation: \n            -> block row, but maintain in redis also, mark that seat unavailabe for 1 mins. \n            -> concurrent request will see if that seat is lock or not. if lock rejec.t\n            -> on ui in that period user will see seat unavaiable.  \n       \n\n      2. optimistic:\n           maintain version column in  seat table. \n             -> read -> do transaction for adding , but add check that version sshould be same \n                with initial else fail. \n             -> problematic in case of many users -> they will try to update and fail -> no blocking here. \n\n            -> maintain the version in row\n            -> allow seat booking but fail at time of updation.  \n             \n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "BVDlCzPcpep3NLGgG-3Hb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4497.6400154519315,
      "y": 1332.2328370031644,
      "width": 830.0633544921875,
      "height": 120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 80,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1671173551,
      "version": 84,
      "versionNonce": 2141211105,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1750486838956,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a system that can collect credentials from multiple financial apps, scrape data, process it, \nand generate analytics for both users and admins. As we discussed, he dynamically added admin-level \nanalysis to the requirements — and I had to adapt the architecture on the fly. It was tricky but fun!⚠️ \nPro Tip: Practice using tools like draw.io or Alphine beforehand — I usually use whiteboards but had to \nquickly adapt during the call.We extended beyond time as I kept pitching scalable ideas (analytics with pie\n charts, generic services, etc.).That persistence paid off — we ended up discussing:",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a system that can collect credentials from multiple financial apps, scrape data, process it, \nand generate analytics for both users and admins. As we discussed, he dynamically added admin-level \nanalysis to the requirements — and I had to adapt the architecture on the fly. It was tricky but fun!⚠️ \nPro Tip: Practice using tools like draw.io or Alphine beforehand — I usually use whiteboards but had to \nquickly adapt during the call.We extended beyond time as I kept pitching scalable ideas (analytics with pie\n charts, generic services, etc.).That persistence paid off — we ended up discussing:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nAQg996OkeiGRkjbvfY9v",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4545.057502831288,
      "y": 1524.8885430788491,
      "width": 426.3675537109375,
      "height": 1520,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 80,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1937680769,
      "version": 1254,
      "versionNonce": 1781932015,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1750488814429,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "functional requirements: \n\n- credentials -> lets assume this is as user metadata. \n- ELT -> db\n- api. to get the analytics result\n\n\n1. analytics ? \nfilter ? \ntime range ? \n\non UI how will it happen. \n\nuser set time range -> metric. \n\nexample of metric on UI and what getting in events. \n\n\nnfr:\n1. scalable.\n2. offline or near real time ?? \n3. approximation ??  -> event loss\n4. idempotency, consistency. \n5. alerts and monitoring. \n\n\nestimations: \n1. traffic of events total from apps -> qps ~\n2. qps -> for analytics query -> read query. ??\n3. storage -> later on . -> qps * roughsize * (5 year)\n\n\nentity:\n\nEvent: \n\n{\n   userId: <>\n   appName: <>\n   ....\n} \n\nA Metric: \n\n- userId\n- data value\n- createdTime\n- timestamp.\n- type: second, min, hour\n- updatedtime\n\n\nApi design: \n\n/api/analytics/metricA ? stateTime=\"\"&&endTime=\"\"\n\nGET -> 2xx, 4xx,5xxx\n\nhttps:\n\nheader\nx-token: \nx-trace:\n\nResponse: {\n\ndataPoints: [{ timestamp, value, id, tags: },....]\n\n}\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "functional requirements: \n\n- credentials -> lets assume this is as user metadata. \n- ELT -> db\n- api. to get the analytics result\n\n\n1. analytics ? \nfilter ? \ntime range ? \n\non UI how will it happen. \n\nuser set time range -> metric. \n\nexample of metric on UI and what getting in events. \n\n\nnfr:\n1. scalable.\n2. offline or near real time ?? \n3. approximation ??  -> event loss\n4. idempotency, consistency. \n5. alerts and monitoring. \n\n\nestimations: \n1. traffic of events total from apps -> qps ~\n2. qps -> for analytics query -> read query. ??\n3. storage -> later on . -> qps * roughsize * (5 year)\n\n\nentity:\n\nEvent: \n\n{\n   userId: <>\n   appName: <>\n   ....\n} \n\nA Metric: \n\n- userId\n- data value\n- createdTime\n- timestamp.\n- type: second, min, hour\n- updatedtime\n\n\nApi design: \n\n/api/analytics/metricA ? stateTime=\"\"&&endTime=\"\"\n\nGET -> 2xx, 4xx,5xxx\n\nhttps:\n\nheader\nx-token: \nx-trace:\n\nResponse: {\n\ndataPoints: [{ timestamp, value, id, tags: },....]\n\n}\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WhKZdOt2mHW6Uv53q3IQW",
