      "seed": 965595439,
      "version": 27,
      "versionNonce": 1607119983,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1750489129374,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This round was with an SDE-2, I was asked to build a rider onboarding application. First 15-20 mins\nwent for discussing the requirements and defining the scope of the problem. Then I was asked to\ndecide between SQL and NoSQL database. I was grilled thorughly for every decision i took. Then,\ndiscussion went into internal details of Amazon Dynamo Db, types of indexes it has and how i would\ndefine tables for this usecase and defining Partition Key & Sort Key for each table. At the end, I\nwas asked on ways to reduce latency in Http Server, had discussions on Status Code based Retries,\nLong & Short Polling.\nThis round went for 75 mins and got positive feedback from the interviewer.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This round was with an SDE-2, I was asked to build a rider onboarding application. First 15-20 mins went for discussing the requirements and defining the scope of the problem. Then I was asked to decide between SQL and NoSQL database. I was grilled thorughly for every decision i took. Then, discussion went into internal details of Amazon Dynamo Db, types of indexes it has and how i would define tables for this usecase and defining Partition Key & Sort Key for each table. At the end, I was asked on ways to reduce latency in Http Server, had discussions on Status Code based Retries, Long & Short Polling.\nThis round went for 75 mins and got positive feedback from the interviewer.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
